  "content": {
    "title": "NC State sends Tennessee women packing in first round of NCAA Tournament",
    "text": "Updated March 20, 2026, 11:02 p.m. ETNo. 7-seed North Carolina State will advance to the second round of the women's NCAA Tournament after defeating No. 10-seed Tennessee, 76-61, at the Crisler Center in Ann Arbor, Michigan on March 20.NC State was led by sophomore guard Zamareya Jones who scored 30 points on 9-of-15 shooting, including 2-of-5 from deep and 10-of-13 from the free throw line. The Wolfpack survived an injury to junior guard Zoe Brooks, who went down with an apparent right leg injury with 5:02 left in the third period.NC State led by seven when she left the game, but leaned on Jones and others to finish the job.\"I have always been a dog, I am too small to play, so having that chip on my shoulder, whether we are winning or not,\" Jones said. \"I have that confidence, so I am going to come out to win every night.\"Tennessee entered the contest with a 35-2 all-time record in the first round before today.The loss marks the third time in Lady Volunteers' basketball program history that they were eliminated from the big dance in the first round, the first time since 2019. Tennessee was also eliminated in the first round of the NCAA Tournament in 2009.For the Lady Volunteers, March Madness has felt more like March Sadness. Tennessee hasn't won a single game in March, finishing the season losing eight-consecutive games. The Lady Vols last win came against Missouri on Feb. 12. They finished the season with a 16-14 record, the lowest win total in a single season in program history.USA TODAY Studio IX: Check out our women's sports hub for in-depth analysis, commentary and more Does NC State hang on in the fourth quarter?The Wolfpack has been able to separate themselves in the fourth quarter extending their lead to as many as 14 with under six minutes left in the game. North Carolina State led by 67-44 with 4:44 remaining.NC State would go on to win the game and advance to the next round. What does a Lady Vols loss mean?Heading into the fourth quarter, No. 10 Tennessee found themselves in jeopardy of a first round exit from the NCAA women's basketball tournament after going down by nine against the No. 7 NC State Wolfpack.A first round for the Lady Vols would be their third-time ever in program history, and the first time since 2019. Tennessee was also eliminated in the first round of the NCAA Tournament in 2009. Tennessee finds themselves trailing NC State at halfThe Lady Volunteers were down 40-29 at halftime as North Carolina State made the most of their opportunities in the first two quarters of play.No. 10 Tennessee has outscored No. 7 NC State, 14-6, in the first five minutes of the third quarter.NC State junior guard Zoe Brooks went down with an apparent right leg injury with 5:02 left in the period. She made a drive to the basket and as she made a jab step, she tweaked her leg. She was able to walk back to the locker room, but has not returned to the game.The Wolfpack held a seven-point lead at the time of Brooks' injury. She left the game with eight points on 3-of-7 shooting and a perfect 2-of-2 from the free throw line.Wolfpack guard Khamil Pierre ended the Lady Vols run with a mid-range jumper. Tennessee responded with a Mia Pauldo 23-foot three point jumper off of a Talaysia Cooper assist to pull within two, 48-46.Both teams traded baskets, as NC State sophomore guard Zamareya Jones knocked down a 26-foot three point jumper before Lady Vols layup by senior forward Zee Spearman.The Wolfpack were able to get themselves to the charity stripe in back-to-back possessions, making all four. They extended their lead to nine at the end of the third quarter, 57-48.What time is Tennessee vs North Carolina State first-round game?No. 7 North Carolina State vs No. 10 Tennessee tips off at 8:00 PM (EST) on Friday, March 20 from Crisler Center (Ann Arbor, Michigan).What channel is Tennessee vs North Carolina State first-round game?No. 7 North Carolina State vs No. 10 Tennessee is airing live on ESPN.How to stream Tennessee vs North Carolina State first-round gameNo. 7 North Carolina State vs No. 10 Tennessee is available to stream on Fubo.Watch the NCAA Tournament all March long with FuboWomen's March Madness schedule todaySee the schedule, live scores and resultsfor all of Friday's NCAA Tournament action here.2026 Women's NCAA Tournament full scheduleMarch 18-19: First FourMarch 20-21: First RoundMarch 22-23: Second RoundMarch 27-28: Sweet 16March 29-30: Elite 8April 3: Final FourApril 5: National ChampionshipJoin the USA TODAY Survivor Pool to win cash prizes",
